<body>
    <h1>SSH Access in IGEL OS 12</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <p>
<style>[data-colorid=3Daotfr7th9e]{color:#202124} html[data-color-mode=3Dda=
rk] [data-colorid=3Daotfr7th9e]{color:#dbdcdf}</style>This article shows ho=
w to configure <span data-colorid=3D"aotfr7th9e">Secure Shell</span> (SSH) =
access to the device in IGEL OS.</p>
<hr>
<p>Menu path: <strong>System &gt; Remote Access &gt; SSH Access</strong></p=
>
<p></p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper image-left-wrapper c=
onfluence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image con=
fluence-content-image-border image-left" width=3D"468" loading=3D"lazy" src=
=3D"99c55ddb4f1037949816ff4711616bea8d06292fcc79aeb14ac7d9b443f71f8b" data-=
image-src=3D"https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/wiki/download/attachments/7330=
2060/image-2024-4-30_11-50-50.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D171636=
4681983&amp;cacheVersion=3D1&amp;api=3Dv2" data-height=3D"577" data-width=
=3D"1280" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"73=
308683" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"att=
achment" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"image-2024-4-30_11-50-50.png=
" data-base-url=3D"https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/wiki" data-linked-resour=
ce-content-type=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"73302060=
" data-linked-resource-container-version=3D"4" data-media-id=3D"e0d1fd8d-86=
2f-46a1-951f-b2a44d2fabc7" data-media-type=3D"file" height=3D"210"></span>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Enable</strong></p>
<p>=E2=98=91&nbsp;The SSH service is enabled.</p>
<p>=E2=98=90 The SSH service is disabled. (Default)<br></p>
<p>If SSH access is enabled, you can configure the following:</p>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Permit empty passwords</strong></p>
<p>=E2=98=91 Logging on without a password is allowed.</p>
<p>=E2=98=90&nbsp;Logging on without a password is not allowed. (Default)<b=
r></p>
<p><strong>Permit administrator logon</strong></p>
<p>=E2=98=91 Logging on as an administrator is allowed.</p>
<p>=E2=98=90 Logging on as an administrator is not allowed. (Default)<br></=
p>
<p><strong>Port number</strong></p>
<p>Port number for SSH. (Default:&nbsp;22)</p>
<p></p>
<p><strong>User Access</strong></p>
<p>List of configured users.</p>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro confluence-information-macro-inf=
ormation">
<span class=3D"aui-icon aui-icon-small aui-iconfont-info confluence-informa=
tion-macro-icon"></span>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro-body">
<p>Unlike&nbsp;<strong>root</strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>user</strong>, t=
he&nbsp;<strong>ruser</strong> is not intended for real SSH sessions, but o=
nly for starting X applications that are listed below under <strong>Applica=
tions Access for Remote User =E2=80=9Cruser=E2=80=9D</strong>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<p>To manage the list:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>User name</strong></p></li>
</ul>
<p style=3D"margin-left: 30.0px;">Permitted user</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Hostname</strong></p></li>
</ul>
<p style=3D"margin-left: 30.0px;">Name of the host from which SSH access ta=
kes place (example:&nbsp;<code>xterm.igel.de</code>)<br></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Deny</strong></p></li>
</ul>
<p>=E2=98=91 Access is denied.</p>
<p>=E2=98=90 Access is allowed. (Default)</p>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro confluence-information-macro-inf=
ormation">
<span class=3D"aui-icon aui-icon-small aui-iconfont-info confluence-informa=
tion-macro-icon"></span>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro-body">
<p>For <code>ruser</code> a password has to be assigned under&nbsp;<strong>=
Security &gt; Password</strong>. The names <code>root</code> and <code>user=
</code> work also without passwords. For more information, see <a href=3D"h=
ttps://igel-jira.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/IGELOS12BSDOCE/pages/73302358/Pa=
ssword+and+User+Types+in+IGEL+OS+12" data-linked-resource-id=3D"73302358" d=
ata-linked-resource-version=3D"7" data-linked-resource-type=3D"page">Passwo=
rd and User Types in IGEL OS 12</a> .</p>
</div>
</div>
<p><br><strong>Permit X11 forwarding</strong></p>
<p>=E2=98=91 &nbsp;X11 forwarding is enabled.</p>
<p>=E2=98=90 &nbsp;X11 forwarding is disabled. (Default)</p>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Applications Access for Remote User =E2=80=9Cruser=E2=80=9D</str=
ong></p>
<p>The <code>ruser</code> is not intended for real SSH sessions, but only f=
or starting X applications configured below. By default these are&nbsp;<cod=
e>localshell</code>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<code>/config/sessions/setup0</code>.</p>
<p></p>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro confluence-information-macro-inf=
ormation">
<span class=3D"aui-icon aui-icon-small aui-iconfont-info confluence-informa=
tion-macro-icon"></span>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro-body">
<p>If you try to log on to the device as <strong>ruser</strong>&nbsp;via SS=
H, then you will never be able to connect. The connection will be closed im=
mediately without anything happening. In this case you must add the paramet=
er "-X" and the program to be started in the session call, like in this exa=
mple:&nbsp;</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: text; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">ssh -X =
ruser@192.168.10.203 localshell</pre>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p></p>
<p>To manage the list:</p>
<div class=3D"error">
<span class=3D"error">Unable to render {include}</span> The included page c=
ould not be found.
</div>
<p><br></p>
<div class=3D"error">
<span class=3D"error">Unable to render {include}</span> The included page c=
ould not be found.
</div>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Command line</strong></p></li>
</ul>
<p style=3D"margin-left: 30.0px;">Command that is allowed or prohibited for=
 the remote user</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Enable application</strong></p></li>
</ul>
<p>=E2=98=91 The application given under <strong>Command line</strong>&nbsp=
;may be executed by the remote user. (Default)</p>
<p>=E2=98=90 The application given under <strong>Command line</strong>&nbsp=
;may not be executed by the remote user.</p>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
